#latest just moves forward with every push — no way to go back to a specific version. A tag like 1.0.0 is a fixed point you can always pull again.
#Convention — major.minor.patch (semantic versioning):

#patch (1.0.1) — bug fix
#minor (1.1.0) — new feature, backwards compatible
#major (2.0.0) — breaking change